The environment as POSIX says: setenv and unsetenv fail a name that is
null, empty or has '=' in it with EINVAL; setenv and putenv fail with
ENOMEM when memory runs out and leave the environment as it was, as in
musl (mlibc's grew a frg::vector, which cannot fail); unsetenv takes
out every string for the name, in place, without allocating; clearenv
leaves an empty environment that setenv can add to (libc-test's
functional/env and regression/setenv-oom). Meant for upstream.

